Robot models redistributed under robots/

- MuJoCo Menagerie (Google DeepMind): the ALOHA 2 model under
  robots/aloha2-nominal/ (BSD-3-Clause, upstream commit da76818e) and the
  SO-101 / SO-ARM100 model under robots/so101-nominal/ (Apache-2.0).
- microduck (Pollen Robotics, microduck_rl, branch develop at d424a0c8,
  Apache-2.0): robot_walk.xml and the 38 meshes it references, under
  robots/microduck/.
- Robotiq 2F-85 (Robotiq Inc., robotiq/isaacsim_assets at 6d992b6,
  CC-BY-4.0): the USD asset imported through Newton into the MuJoCo bundle
  under robots/robotiq-2f85-isaac/. "Robotiq" is Robotiq Inc.'s name; this
  project is not affiliated with Robotiq. The bundle schema string
  `robotiq-actuator-bundle/1` is a frozen format identifier, not a claim.
- Unitree Go2 (Unitree Robotics, unitreerobotics/unitree_rl_mjlab,
  Apache-2.0): go2.xml and its meshes, fetched into a project's bundle by
  the onboarding step; the declared actuator constants in
  trainnr-mjlab/src/trainnr_mjlab/go2_walk.py are read from the same
  repository (go2_constants.py at 1425b15) and cited there.

Actuator models under robots/actuators/

- BAM (Rhoban; Duclusaud, Passault, Padois, Ly, ICRA 2025; Apache-2.0):
  the fitted actuator parameters for the Dynamixel MX-64, MX-106, XL-320,
  XL-330, the Feetech STS3215, the Waveshare ST3025 and the eRob 80 series,
  each wrapped with a PROVENANCE.json naming the source, the citation and
  the licence. The xl330-refit bundle carries numbers fitted by us on BAM's
  published bench logs, whose own licence is unstated on their bucket; the
  logs are not redistributed.

Datasets and scenes used for the published results (not redistributed)

- Public Unitree Go2 telemetry: YibinWu/leg-odometry (release test_v1.0),
  DFKI's field recording on Zenodo (record 19336009) and IIT's in-air log.
  The registry trainnr/trainnr/robots/public_logs.py records each log's
  licence state (unlabelled where the publisher states none); only
  measurements derived from them are kept here.
- Mip-NeRF 360 (Barron et al., CVPR 2022): the garden capture's 185 stills,
  taken from nvs-bench/mipnerf360 on Hugging Face into a local project under
  the dataset's own terms; the repository keeps one rendering of the twin
  in that scene and the evaluation rows.
- Neverwhere (MIT): the Go1 parkour scenes imported into a local project
  for the see-versus-touch gap measurement; the repository keeps the
  numbers.

Software used as dependencies (no source copied)

- MuJoCo and MuJoCo Warp (Google DeepMind, Apache-2.0); mjlab (mujocolab,
  Apache-2.0); rsl_rl (ETH Zurich Robotic Systems Lab, BSD-3-Clause);
  Gymnasium (Farama Foundation, MIT); LeRobot (Hugging Face, Apache-2.0;
  trainnr/trainnr/envs/lerobot_plugin.py implements its EnvConfig
  interface); gym-aloha / ACT (Tony Z. Zhao et al.; Apache-2.0 / MIT): the
  transfer-cube task in trainnr/trainnr/tasks/aloha2.py follows the
  original simulator's conventions so released checkpoints see the scene
  they were trained on.
- Rerun (Rerun Technologies, MIT OR Apache-2.0): the Python SDK, and the
  viewer embedded in the Studio through the re_viewer and re_ui
  crates; egui and eframe (emilk, MIT OR Apache-2.0).
- Newton (NVIDIA, Apache-2.0) and OpenUSD (Pixar, Apache-2.0 with the
  Tomorrow Open Source Technology notice): the USD import door.
- gsplat (Apache-2.0), COLMAP (BSD-3-Clause, a system install) and Open3D
  (MIT): the scene capture chain.
- The NeurIPS 2023 LaTeX style (neurips_2023.sty, the NeurIPS Foundation),
  beside the paper's generated main.tex, for the preprint's layout only.
